    {
      "id": "c12_m_6",
      "name": "Application of Derivatives",
      "keyPoints": [
        "First Derivative Test: Evaluated in neighborhood $(c-h, c+h)$. If $f'(x)$ changes $+ \\to -$ $\\implies$ Local Maxima at $c$. If $f'(x)$ changes $- \\to +$ $\\implies$ Local Minima at $c$. No sign change $\\implies$ Point of Inflection.",
        "Second Derivative Test: $f'(c) = 0$ and $f''(c) < 0 \\implies$ Local Maxima at $c$. $f'(c) = 0$ and $f''(c) > 0 \\implies$ Local Minima at $c$. $f''(c) = 0 \\implies$ Test Fails.",
        "Absolute Extrema on $[a, b]$: Evaluate $f(x)$ at all critical points and boundaries."
      ],
      "keyDerivations": [],
      "formulas": [
        {
          "id": "fm_6_1",
          "chapter": "Application of Derivatives",
          "name": "Rate of Change",
          "latex": "\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{dy/dt}{dx/dt}",
          "tags": []
        },
